Existing rows get the time the `ALTER` ran, because on PG 11+ a stable default is evaluated once and applied to all current rows. If you'd rather have existing rows as `NULL` or backfilled from something else, add the column as nullable without `NOT NULL`, backfill, then set the default and constraint afterwards:

```sql
ALTER TABLE orders ADD COLUMN created_at timestamp without time zone;
-- backfill here
ALTER TABLE orders ALTER COLUMN created_at SET DEFAULT (now() AT TIME ZONE 'Europe/London');
ALTER TABLE orders ALTER COLUMN created_at SET NOT NULL;
```

